{"name":"Garden Shed","hex":"#d6efda","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden shed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A toolshed in a garden or allotment, holding gardening equipment.","Homespun; mom-and-pop."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden_shed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shed","blocks":[{"text":"A shed is typically a simple, single-storey roofed structure, often used for storage, for hobbies, or as a workshop, and typically serving as outbuilding, such as in a back garden or on an allotment. Sheds vary considerably in their size and complexity of construction, from simple open-sided ones designed to cover bicycles or garden items to large wood-framed structures with shingled roofs, windows, and electrical outlets. Sheds used on farms or in the industry can be large structures. The main types of shed construction are metal sheathing over a metal frame, plastic sheathing and frame, all-wood construction, and vinyl-sided sheds built over a wooden frame. Small sheds may include a wooden or plastic floor, while more permanent ones may be built on a concrete pad or foundation. Sheds may be lockable to deter theft or entry by children, domestic animals, wildlife, etc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Schuppen_7235.jpg/330px-Schuppen_7235.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shed","wikidata":"Q721931"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&